{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.opposite_sides_of_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.opposite_sides_of_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CompleteStructureExclusion.lean#L133-L164","doc":"**The sign flip needs more than nonvanishing.**  `Im V₄₁` is positive inside\nthe cone `|Im u| < |Re u|` and negative outside it, so two anchors of OPPOSITE\nleak sign must lie on opposite sides of the diagonal `|Re u| = |Im u|` — not\nmerely away from `0`.\n\nRecorded as the sharper A_ω-free filter that `qou-8vt2` AV4 and `qou-qmnb` AV1\ntell candidates to apply BEFORE computing any magnitude.\n\n**Statement note.**  An earlier version of this claimed the stronger ordering\n`Im₂² − Re₂² < Re₁² − Im₁²`, and `linarith` rejected it — correctly.  Both\nquantities are positive, but opposite SIGNS of the leak give no ORDERING between\ntheir magnitudes.  What is true, and all that is true, is the sidedness below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.both_anchors_deformed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.both_anchors_deformed","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CompleteStructureExclusion.lean#L122-L131","doc":"**Both anchors at once.**  Two channels — the muon and proton anchors — with\nnonzero measured leaks both have nonzero deformation.  Stated because the\nexclusion is about the PAIR: a single anchor could be argued away as a\nnormalisation choice, both cannot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.u_ne_zero_of_S_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.u_ne_zero_of_S_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CompleteStructureExclusion.lean#L111-L120","doc":"**The measured leak forces a nonzero deformation.**  Contrapositive of the\nabove: since `S ≠ 0` is measured at both anchors, `u(q₀) ≠ 0` there.\n\nThis is the exclusion.  The anchors' own hyperbolic structures ARE the complete\nones (regular ideal cell, proved in the angle-structure files), and the complete\nstructure is `u = 0`; so `u` cannot be the anchor's own NZ deformation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.S_eq_zero_of_u_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.S_eq_zero_of_u_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CompleteStructureExclusion.lean#L103-L109","doc":"**A channel sitting at the complete structure has no leak.**\nIf the deformation map sends the substrate point to `u = 0`, the S-leak is\nidentically zero, whatever the Stokes constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.imV₄₁_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CompleteStructureExclusion.imV₄₁_zero","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CompleteStructureExclusion.lean#L97-L101","doc":"**The Chern-Simons part vanishes at the complete structure.**\n`Im V₄₁ 0 = κ·(0² − 0²) = 0` — immediate from the harmonic form, recorded\nseparately because it is the hinge of everything below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}